# Marker-directed panel composition plan

Goal: recover the separating line and indicated side in public parent 7491f3cf,
then compose panels under marker_first|marker_second without altering earlier
panels. Generalize table layout while retaining geometric inference.

1. Failing official-label and topology tests; implement independent Python oracle,
   general protected-Racket reference, and exact canonical native copy.
2. Failing count/grammar/privacy tests; implement generator and native adapter,
   matched settings, 2–6 demos and four private queries including a 30×30 table.
3. Finite adversarial audit: marker omission, 8-neighbor leakage, straight-line
   approximation, fixed-side rules, wrong boundary arbitration and whole-panel
   merges. Retain and repair concrete failures.
4. Authoring preflight, maximum-count protected labels, source-bound wrong-region
   causal replay, public export validation, focused/staged tests, relocated smoke.
5. Inventory and compact return. Owner registration/qualification remain separate.

Architecture: table parsing -> mask-line 8-components -> 4-connected flood from
hint across the complement -> source selection and boundary overlay -> final
panel reconstruction. Alternate swaps the two sides, not the core inference.
